# Mean Mr Mustard, verse (figure 186.1)
# Fourteen bars, 4 + 6 + 4. In the middle phrase Pollack types the bassline with a beat row above
# it (1 2 3& 4 &): the bass climbs B C C# D and later falls C# C B in eighths on the "&" of 3, 4
# and the "&" of 4, so the D and B chords arrive in the bass just before their downbeats.
# Added: the bass B in the first bar of the middle phrase (he starts typing the bass in its second
# bar, on the downbeat B). The "1" over the B chord's first bar is kept in the beat row.
#? Bass octave (B2 up to D3) is a choice for range; check against the record.
